Build cloud sync of saved passwords (passwordApiVersion 1).

The shell syncs Chromium's saved passwords between the user's HarmonyOS
devices through its own table and Cloud Space, and asks the engine for a
snapshot with plain text, writes by site and username, and a notice when
the store changes. That lives in
chrome/browser/ui/ohos/shell_password_sync_ohos.cc, an overlay file; this
adds it to the build next to the other shell files, with the password
store target it reads StoredCredential from.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
and the incremental patches before it applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-password-sync.patch

diff --git a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
index bff28c7..8ac05cb 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -1734,6 +1734,7 @@ source_set("core") {
       "ui/ohos/shell_extensions_ohos.cc",
       "ui/ohos/shell_extensions_ohos.h",
       "ui/ohos/shell_passwords_ohos.cc",
+      "ui/ohos/shell_password_sync_ohos.cc",
     ]
     # HUKS keeps the OSCrypt key, and the common-event subscription ends the
     # re-authentication window when the screen locks.
@@ -1748,6 +1749,8 @@ source_set("core") {
       "//components/user_data_importer/content",
       "//components/os_crypt/browser:posix_key_provider",
       "//components/printing/browser/print_to_pdf",
+      # Password sync reads and writes the store's StoredCredential directly.
+      "//components/password_manager/core/browser/password_store:password_store_interface",
     ]
   }
 
